        "original_id": "c01145c5-f2a5-59a8-9e3a-7cc2bf2dabf0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: 41st Tactical Squadron, 22nd Air Base, German Luftwaffe, Mikoyan design bureau\n- Products: Mikoyan MiG-29, Sukhoi Su-27, McDonnell Douglas F-15 Eagle, General Dynamics F-16 Fighting Falcon\n- Concepts: air superiority fighter\n\nFacts:\n- During the 1970s, the Mikoyan design bureau developed the Mikoyan MiG-29 in the Soviet Union as an air superiority fighter.\n- During the 1970s, the Mikoyan MiG-29 and the Sukhoi Su-27 were developed to counter the McDonnell Douglas F-15 Eagle and the General Dynamics F-16 Fighting Falcon.\n- The Mikoyan MiG-29 is a twin-engine jet fighter aircraft and has the NATO reporting name Fulcrum.\n- The 41st Tactical Squadron operates Mikoyan MiG-29 jet fighters acquired from the German Luftwaffe.\n- The 22nd Air Base hosts the 41st Air Tactical Squadron as its main unit, and that squadron flies Mikoyan MiG-29 fighters.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
